Mip chains for one level textures: a 2D texture of 8 bit colour or DXT with a single level is made BGRA with a whole
mip chain, its level decoded (DXT too) and halved down to 1 x 1 by 2 x 2 means as it uploads. The title asks to
filter across mip levels on textures that have none, which shimmered in the distance and left anisotropic filtering
nothing to do; draws that filter without mips still read the top level only.

